00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:26.860
Japan is the country with the greatest reason
to be scared of nuclear power.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.250
Think about it, they have the biggest nuclear
trauma record in the world.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:38.370
So far, they are the only country that has
suffered a nuclear attack.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.720
Namely, the Hiroshima and Nagasaki bombings.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.650
In fact, during the 50s, nuclear paranoia
was big in Japan.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:49.230
The most famous outcome of this is the movie
Godzilla, the story of a gigantic radioactive

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.950
lizard that destroys cities.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.860
Nonetheless, as the Japanese economy grew,
Japan started building its own reactors.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.450
A couple of decades later, they became the
third biggest nuclear powerhouse, only surpassed

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.090
by America and France.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.540
Yep, you heard that right.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.100
While European countries like Germany were
organizing all kinds of anti nuclear demonstrations,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:14.330
Japan blindly trusted uranium.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:20.530
But then, while the Japanese were charmed
by atomic power, the unexpected happened.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:26.850
Japan earthquake: Explosion at Fukushima nuclear
plant

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:32.270
A powerful explosion has hit a nuclear power
station in north-eastern Japan which was badly

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.920
damaged in Friday's devastating earthquake
and tsunami.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.840
Overnight, nuclear panic came back to Japan
and the whole world.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.950
And there was a good reason for it.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.080
You see, during the Chernobyl accident in
1986, many people said “the problem isn’t

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.830
nuclear power--it’s the fact that Chernobyl
didn’t follow the security protocols: you

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.830
know the soviets…”

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.670
But Japan is a wealthy country that takes
extreme care with its security.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.690
And despite all this care, Fukushima was still
a disaster.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.620
All of a sudden, Japan shut down all of their
nuclear power plants.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.960
They went from having 30% nuclear power in
their energy mix to a tiny 3%.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.700
So now you might assume that Japan is turning
into an antinuclear country, right?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.770
Well… in fact, the opposite is true!

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:23.569
20-22% share of nuclear power at core of updated
energy policy

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:24.569
Exactly!

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:25.900
Nuclear power has come back to Japan!

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.560
In fact, not only Japan… as we said in previous
videos, the whole Asian continent is going

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.560
through a nuclear revolution.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.910
And when I say the whole continent, I mean
it, from wealthy countries like Japan to poor

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.569
countries like Bangladesh.

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:43.730
And this is surprising if we take into account
that nuclear reactors are far from cheap.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.980
In this other video, we told you what’s
going on in China, but today we’re going

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.440
to focus on what’s happening in the other
two biggest Asian countries, Japan and India.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.400
Because the question we want to address now
is What about nuclear power appeals to Asians

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.400
so much?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.090
And how has India, still a poorer country,
become such a nuclear powerhouse?

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.470
Today, we are going to answer these questions
but, before we do, as always, let’s take

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.900
a look back at the history.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:17.300
THE NUCLEAR GIANT IS BACK
Fukushima meant an immediate nuclear shutdown.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:22.120
The Japanese wanted to minimize risk and stopped
all their reactors basically overnight.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.270
So you might be wondering…

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.780
Where have they gotten their energy since
then?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.120
I mean… how did they replace the energy
input they used to get from nuclear power?

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.690
The answer is a complete ecological HARA KIRI.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:33.770
Yes, you heard that right!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.660
If you thought nuclear power was bad for the
environment…

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:44.250
most of the alternatives are even worse.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.849
Without uranium, Japan had to start using
fossil fuels.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:51.930
This had two consequences: electricity prices
rose 20% because,suddenly, they had to buy

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.180
tons of liquefied natural gas.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.410
The other consequence was that CO2 emissions
skyrocketed.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.250
In other words… if Godzilla happened to
show up in Fukushima… he would have to wear

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.250
a mask.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.840
And I know what you might be thinking…

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.060
Why don’t they use renewable sources?

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.830
What’s the problem with green energy?

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.520
Well… the problem is TIME.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.120
If you wanna have solar panels and wind turbines,
first you have to build them.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.100
And Japan is far behind other countries in
this matter.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:24.300
In fact, it’s only NOW that they’re starting
their green energy plan.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.800
Their goal is to achieve 22% of their energy
from renewable sources by 2030.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.389
For a comparison, Europe plans to achieve
the same in 2020.

00:04:32.389 --> 00:04:33.389
Why?

00:04:33.389 --> 00:04:36.600
Mainly because Europe started investing in
these technologies way sooner.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.600
But not only that!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.949
Even if Japan wanted to speed up their green
energy plan, they couldn’t.

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:43.150
One of their main problems is red tape.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.020
Want to start a wind turbine park?

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.849
You need 5 years of paperwork.

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:50.990
This is three times longer than most industrialized
countries.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.830
And reducing red tape is almost impossible.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.800
And let’s not forget to mention the classic
problem with green energy.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.990
You know, that it’s very expensive to store
electricity using these methods.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.860
For example, solar panels only give you energy
during the day and the same goes for wind

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.099
turbines: you only get energy when it’s
windy.

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:15.169
During a calm night, you still need other
energy sources.

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:20.389
So, realistically, Japan only has two options
for energy: they can keep importing expensive

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:23.590
gas and polluting like crazy or… they can
go nuclear!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:30.089
And… the answer seems like a no brainer
for them…

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:33.629
Japan restarts five nuclear power reactors
in 2018

00:05:33.629 --> 00:05:38.960
In total, at the time we made this video,
Japan has already restarted 9 nuclear reactors.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.909
But it’s not only that they’re restarting
at the capacity they previously had…

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:47.139
They want to build even more!

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:51.849
Process begins at Shimane nuclear plant to
operate new reactor

00:05:51.849 --> 00:05:55.330
You see, when you’re talking about nuclear
power, there’s one important thing you must

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.189
understand: they produce energy on an ongoing
basis.

00:05:58.189 --> 00:06:03.160
This means, from the moment you start a reactor,
you have the same amount of energy every day.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.119
No more, no less…

00:06:05.119 --> 00:06:09.909
This is why nuclear power is considered the
base of an electric system.

00:06:09.909 --> 00:06:13.950
Turning off a nuclear reactor is very expensive
and it’s only done when there’s a real

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.059
risk of an accident.

00:06:15.059 --> 00:06:24.750
This is why they’re always producing energy
and… on top of that nuclear energy is where

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.930
we can add other energy sources like coal,
gas or green energy.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:34.089
These are energy sources that can be adjusted
based on the energy demands on a particular

00:06:34.089 --> 00:06:35.089
day.

00:06:35.089 --> 00:06:38.349
Nonetheless, if we said green energy depends
on the weather, coal or gas depends on market

00:06:38.349 --> 00:06:40.879
prices, which fluctuate daily.

00:06:40.879 --> 00:06:45.220
Nonetheless, you just need a little piece
of uranium to have nuclear power, so price

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:49.389
fluctuations on this material don’t affect
the cost that much.

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:52.479
This is the reason why Japan is going back
to nuclear.

00:06:52.479 --> 00:06:53.479
But not only Japan!

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:58.729
In South Korea, they are also mastering this
form of energy.

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:04.669
While in North Korea they build nukes, their
southern neighbours build reactors.

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:07.050
In total, they have 6.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.050
And now you might wonder…

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:10.539
Who does build those nuclear power plants?

00:07:10.539 --> 00:07:14.539
The truth is nuclear power is really complex
and expensive.

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:17.800
And there are very few companies that master
those technologies.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.659
Do you remember those reactors built by Japan
in the 60s?

00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:23.159
Well, they were built by British and American
companies.

00:07:23.159 --> 00:07:26.610
For years, General Electric and Westinghouse
dominated the market.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:31.589
But, soon, TOSHIBA, HITACHI and MITSUBISHI
started their own generation of models.

00:07:31.589 --> 00:07:32.860
South Korea followed suit.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.629
They started buying American, French and Canadian
models.

00:07:35.629 --> 00:07:40.279
But then, HYUNDAY, DOOSAN and KEPCO started
manufacturing their own reactors.

00:07:40.279 --> 00:07:47.800
Now South Korea is another nuclear powerhouse
that exports technology all over the world.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:53.559
UAE and South Korea celebrate completion of
Barakah's first nuclear reactor

00:07:53.559 --> 00:07:55.050
And now you might wonder…

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.050
OK but…

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:58.409
How much does a nuclear reactor cost?

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:02.209
To give you an idea, all the reactors that
they want to build in the Arabian Peninsula

00:08:02.209 --> 00:08:06.789
cost 20 billion dollars: this is the cost
of an Olympic game.

00:08:06.789 --> 00:08:10.400
Just to make a comparison, a fossil fuel plant
that generates the same amount of energy costs

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.389
20 times less.

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:15.779
Of course, producing a Kilowatt of electricity
with nuclear power is the cheapest way to

00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:16.779
do so.

00:08:16.779 --> 00:08:20.960
But the initial cost is only affordable to
very rich economies.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:21.960
So then…

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.740
How on earth is it possible that India and
Bangladesh can have nuclear reactors?

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:32.900
Let’s have a look!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:37.250
FROM GODZILLA TO GOGOLA
Japan has Godzilla: India has GOGOLA.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.710
If you didn’t know, after the commercial
success of Godzilla, Bollywood created their

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.760
own exploitation version.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:47.550
And this is the giant GOGOLA.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:51.590
But enough with the movies!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.880
When it came to energy, we had the same story.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.070
If Japan had nuclear power plants, India wanted
the same.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.070
The problem?

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.580
American companies didn’t want to sell reactors
to India!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:01.580
Why?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.890
Mainly because India has nukes.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.180
Yes, you heard that right!

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:07.590
The country of Gandhi and non-violence is
one of the few nations with nukes.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:10.620
And their biggest enemy, Pakistan, also has
them.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.740
So there’s a real danger that one day they’ll
want to use them.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.580
In other words, America doesn’t want to
help India go even more nuclear.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:21.530
But that’s not even the most interesting
part!

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:26.030
You see, unlike Japan and South Korea, India
has its own uranium mines.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:30.110
So, since America didn’t want to help them,
they went to France and Russia.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:34.870
This is why many of the nuclear reactors in
India are built by ROSATOM, a Russian company.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.810
But here’s the interesting part!

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:41.080
Indian reactors have something very special
about them: they’re cheaper than anywhere

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.080
else.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.080
Why?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.120
Because they’re the only ones that use NATURAL
URANIUM.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:52.700
You see, most of the world’s reactors use
ENRICHED URANIUM.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.780
This kind of uranium can’t be used to manufacture
bombs.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.470
This is why buying enriched uranium is kind
of easy while there are many restrictions

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.180
on getting natural uranium
Basically, if you go to buy natural uranium,

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.180
they’ll tell you ‘Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait
a minute, cowboy!

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.180
Where are you going with that?

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.180
Do you want to make nukes, huh?

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:09.240
Leave this on the shelf and get outta here!’

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:13.220
But since India has its own uranium, they
can do whatever they want with it.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.440
This is why their natural uranium reactors
are way cheaper.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:21.160
And it explains news like this.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:26.330
India plans tenfold uranium output growth
India is currently building 7 nuclear reactors

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.660
but they plan to build 20 more.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.660
Yes, you heard that right: 20 brand new nuclear
reactors.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.140
As I said, they’re using mainly Russian
technology.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:36.960
And… you know, since Rosatom was doing business
in the region, they went to neighbouring Bangladesh

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:40.030
and made this.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:46.020
Rosatom starts work on unit 2 of Bangladesh
n-project

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.070
With this, Bangladesh will cover 20% of their
energy demands with nuclear power.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.710
And the same is happening with Pakistan.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:56.020
Do you remember our previous video where we
told you China is starting to create its own

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.240
nuclear technology?

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.800
Well, Pakistan is the first one buying from
the Chinese.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:04.060
In other words, nuclear power is not a rich
country business anymore.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.780
Asia is going crazy over it.

